<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Beroz et al. (2018) Nature Physics & Hartmann et al. (2019) Nature Physics 3D rod-cell nematic verticalization and fountain flow in growing Vibrio cholerae biofilms — MorphoEval overall 53.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2019-yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain.py` (overall weighted score: 56.4/100). The v1 script implements the parabolic radial compressive stress profile sigma_rr(r) = kappa*(R^2 - r^2), the inverse cell-length peeling buckling threshold sigma_c(L) = sigma_c0*(L_0/L), and the verticalization front radius r_vert(R, L) = sqrt(R^2 - R_c(L)^2) across the 7-point A22/cephalexin cell-length sweep, but uses a closed-form radial tanh ansatz instead of relaxing a 2D/axisymmetric Landau-de Gennes nematic director & fountain-flow energy functional, omits the 8-point radial expansion trajectory and Delta rbmA / Delta bap1 Delta rbmC adhesion-loss flat-monolayer controls, and does not segment the vendored Vibrio cholerae micrograph (`vibrio_cholerae_biofilm_specimen.jpg`). Overall 53.7/100 (faithfulness 47.4, reproducibility 68.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit e93f00e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 58, Morphological realism / specimen match 35, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 52, Source and data traceability 74, Code-to-model traceability 68, Reproducibility package 64. Output judged: docs/media/vibrio_biofilm_nematic_fountain_comparison.png: rendered output of 2019-yan-vibrio-biofilm-nematic-fountain.py at e93f00e, image/png, 153325 B, 1680×1330 px, artifact_sha256 0bb2af64dcd69827f6ffa1768dfb50fd515c873a4c6e74982ad6bc73ea81f9f5 (sha256 0bb2af64dcd69827f6ffa1768dfb50fd515c873a4c6e74982ad6bc73ea81f9f5), spec_fingerprint d831566c61695d418bb35d8095aa8c6100057ce72fecb5a3fc13843d4bcb5000. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d831566c61695d418bb35d8095aa8c6100057ce72fecb5a3fc13843d4bcb5000; artifact_sha256: 0bb2af64dcd69827f6ffa1768dfb50fd515c873a4c6e74982ad6bc73ea81f9f5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/vibrio_biofilm_nematic_fountain/paper_citations.bib=25b7c5d98c7e6bdc..., datasets/vibrio_biofilm_nematic_fountain/scout_manifest.json=17aa91569cbce80c..., datasets/vibrio_biofilm_nematic_fountain/vibrio_biofilm_nematic_fountain_reference.json=2f8c3198aefc7de1..., datasets/vibrio_biofilm_nematic_fountain/vibrio_cholerae_biofilm_specimen.jpg=d21370a429873aae...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement all 5 genetic and pharmacological controls: wild-type rugose, Delta rbmA cell-cell cohesion mutant, Delta bap1 Delta rbmC substrate-adhesion mutant, A22 short rods, and cephalexin long rods.",
        "remediation needed: Implement both the 7-point A22/WT/cephalexin cell-length sweep L in [1.4, 4.5] um (verifying inverse square-root critical radius scaling R_c ~ L^-0.5) and the 8-point radial expansion trajectory R(t) in [6.0, 25.0] um (verifying r_vert(t) = sqrt(R(t)^2 - R_c^2)).",
        "remediation needed: Replace the closed-form radial tanh ansatz with a 2D/axisymmetric Landau-de Gennes nematic tilt L-BFGS-B free-energy minimizer coupled to 3D fountain-flow dome extrusion H(x,y).",
        "remediation needed: Segment the vendored Public Domain Vibrio cholerae micrograph (`vibrio_cholerae_biofilm_specimen.jpg`) to extract individual rod cells, empirical aspect ratio L/d, and 2D nematic orientation order, and enforce runtime SHA-256 verification." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.37e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

